"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Commercial & HOA Claim Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Roof & Hail Damage Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/hail-roof-damage-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wind, Tornado & Derecho Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/tornado-straight-line-wind-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Water Damage Claim Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/water-damage-claim-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Claim Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Black Hills Wildfire Claim Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/black-hills-wildfire-claim-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Blizzard, Ice & Snow Load Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/blizzard-ice-snow-load-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Farm & Ranch Building Appraisal","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/farm-ranch-outbuilding-appraiser/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance Estimate Review","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/insurance-estimate-second-opinion/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/appraiser-services/umpire-and-neutral-appraiser/"}}]},"knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Hail damage","Derecho and wind damage","Wildfire claims","Coinsurance"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"South Dakota Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#webpage","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/","name":"Insurance Appraisal Process in South Dakota | 7 Steps","description":"The insurance appraisal process in South Dakota, step by step: the written demand, both appraisers, the umpire and the binding award explained.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-14","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#primaryimage","url":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/policy-review.webp","width":1024,"height":683},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#howto"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal process","item":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/"}],"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How the insurance appraisal process works in South Dakota","description":"The seven stages of a property insurance appraisal, from the disagreement to the signed award.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Pin down the disagreement","text":"Appraisal starts with a specific dispute about the amount of loss. Before anything else, compare the carrier’s itemized estimate with your own and list the differences: missing slopes, short quantities, pricing, matching, code items. If the dispute is really about coverage, appraisal is the wrong tool."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Send the written demand","text":"Either side can demand appraisal in writing under most policies. The demand should identify the claim, state that you disagree on the amount of loss and invoke the appraisal provision. Keep proof of delivery. Some policies set a time for each side to name its appraiser after the demand."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Each side names an appraiser","text":"You choose your appraiser and the insurer chooses its own. Most clauses require each appraiser to be competent and independent or disinterested. Your appraiser inspects the property, builds a line-item estimate and gets ready to defend it."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"The appraisers select an umpire","text":"The two appraisers try to agree on a neutral umpire. If they cannot within the time the policy allows, either side can usually ask a court where the property is located to appoint one."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"The appraisers work the numbers","text":"Your appraiser and the carrier’s appraiser meet, inspect together if needed and go through the estimates line by line. Every item they agree on is settled. Many claims resolve entirely at this stage."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"The umpire decides what is left","text":"Items the appraisers cannot agree on go to the umpire with photos, measurements and pricing support. The umpire may inspect the property and will decide each open item."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"Two signatures make the award","text":"When any two of the three panel members sign the award, it sets the amount of loss. The award should list replacement cost and actual cash value clearly. The carrier then pays according to the policy, applying the deductible, limits and any prior payments."}],"@id":"https://southdakotainsuranceappraiser.com/inside-the-appraisal-process/#howto"}]}</script>
